        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: aee75ec93771eedc6391a141a5fbdc3613409dcba611e39db2e0be67f47b8953\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: 4c0e0c18d65fff727a5b64c39e6abf1a901b589d5c89cda1667b6e7aed58b215\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Step 1: Configure a local account with the necessary privilege level to troubleshoot network outage and restore operations as shown in the following example: \n\nRP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config)#username xxxxxxxxx group netadmin \nRP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config)#username xxxxxxxxx secret xxxxxx\n\nStep 2: Configure the authentication order to use the local account if the authentication server is not reachable as shown in the following example:\n\nRP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config)#aaa authentication login default group tacacs+ local",
          "group_id": "V-216530",
          "group_id_src": "V-216530",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000148-NDM-000346",
          "rule_id": "SV-216530r1051115_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-216530r1051115_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco router must be configured with only one local account to be used as the account of last resort in the event the authentication server is unavailable.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-ND-000490",
          "severity": "medium",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "21cd59c1-cf93-5622-b028-c123279563f9",
